  "summary": "New generators add pharmacophore, pocket and conjugate constraints, while HEDGEHOG and PBPK re-scoring show that standard metrics miss attrition and exposure effects.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is constraint-conditioned generation paired with more demanding evaluation. PharmaDiff conditions 3D diffusion on pharmacophores, PFM applies a perturbed conditional probability path in pocket-conditioned flow matching, and CupOFMoCA enforces cross-component chemical constraints in discrete flows for PROTAC and peptide-drug conjugate assembly. The newer element is evaluation. HEDGEHOG applies six filtration stages to 22 generators on KRAS G12D and finds stage-wise attrition that standard metrics miss. PBPK simulations on PARP1 candidates show that dose-driven exposure and safety limits reshuffle which molecules look promising. Together these items point to downstream criteria, not docking-style scores alone, as the basis for judging generators. The summaries here report no experimental validation of generated molecules.",
